extra.reason:
Closed without migration. Reading GPUProcessPreferences.cpp confirms there is nothing GPU-process-side to convert:

  void GPUProcessPreferences::copyEnabledWebPreferences(const WebPreferences& webPreferences)
  {
  #if ENABLE(VP9)
      if (webPreferences.vp9DecoderEnabled())
          vp9DecoderEnabled = true;
      if (webPreferences.sWVPDecodersAlwaysEnabled())
          swVPDecodersAlwaysEnabled = true;
  #endif
  }

The single member function is only called from Source/WebKit/UIProcess/GPU/GPUProcessProxy.cpp:817 -- it runs in the UI process before sending the IPC message. It does not execute inside the GPU process at all, so converting it would not advance the "no C++ in the GPU process" goal of the larger transformation. The GPUProcessPreferences struct itself has to stay C++ regardless because the autogen needs it as the IPC argument type.

If/when the UI process is ever Swiftified, this two-line helper rolls in for free with that work.
